Configuration:
1. Preferences → Package Settings → Kubeseal → Settings
2. Fill "stages" with per-cluster cert_path / private_key_path (see defaults)
3. Run "Kubeseal: Validate Configuration"

Usage:
- Encrypt selection or whole file → Ctrl+K, Ctrl+E
  → quick panel asks which stage key to use
  → no selection: seals Secret template → sibling *-sealedsecret.yaml
  → selection: raw --raw encrypt only inside a SealedSecret (encryptedData)
- Decrypt selection → Ctrl+K, Ctrl+D
  → asks which stage private key to use
  → Secret.data values are auto base64-decoded

Safety:
- Refuses full-file re-seal of an existing SealedSecret
- Refuses raw string encrypt unless the open buffer is kind: SealedSecret
  (plain Secret → clear selection and full-file seal instead)
- Refuses empty Secret templates (no data / stringData values)
- Caps input size (2 MiB) and subprocess timeout (5–300s)
- If *-sealedsecret.yaml already exists: auto-rename to .bckp-<oldName> then
  atomic write (temp + replace; timestamp suffix if .bckp- already present)
- Private keys that are group/world-readable are rejected (chmod 600)
- Decrypt confirms non-ciphertext selections and prod-named stages
- Reseal / YAML-decrypt warnings use a **quick panel**
  (same UI family as Cmd+Shift+P — keyboard: arrows + Enter / Esc)
- Decrypt opens a scratch buffer (harder to accidentally commit plaintext)
- Concurrent encrypt/decrypt operations are blocked

note: if namespace / secret name is missing from the file metadata, you will be prompted.
